<task id="043" project="email-communication-solution-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>Deploy Communication PCFs (Connections + Actions) + OOB form config + pack "Awaiting Association" view + remove deployed Send ribbon; UI verification</title>
    <phase>Wave 4 — OOB form + PCFs (deploy)</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>6</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>042, 044</dependencies>
    <blocks>060</blocks>
    <tags>pcf, deploy, dataverse, e2e-test</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Deploys two user-visible PCFs to Dataverse, configures the OOB sprk_communication form, removes a deployed ribbon button, and runs browser UI tests; outward-facing regression surface; FULL Step 9.5 gates.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W4</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>NFR-07</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    RE-TARGETED by the W4 pivot (2026-07-15 — see `notes/W4-architecture-pivot-oob-form-pcf.md`): this is no longer a Code Page deploy. Deploy the two PCFs built in W4 — **CommunicationConnections** (task 042, multi-association review) and **CommunicationActions** (task 044, Reply/Forward/Send/Save/Save-to-SharePoint) — to Dataverse and configure the OOB `sprk_communication` model-driven form:

    1. **Build + package** both PCFs (`npm run build:prod` in each; already clean) into solution(s) — mirror the `RegardingResolver/Solution/` packaging pattern (solution.xml + customizations.xml + Controls/ + pack.ps1) or `pac solution` equivalent.
    2. **Place both PCFs on the OOB form**: CommunicationConnections bound to `sprk_associationprovenance` (+ `sprk_associationstatus`) in the right ~34% "accessories" column (alongside the existing RegardingResolver); CommunicationActions bound to `sprk_communicationtype` in the form header/command area. Supply the Actions PCF auth-config inputs (apiBaseUrl / clientAppId / bffAppId) from Dataverse environment variables.
    3. **Pack the "Communications Awaiting Association" view** authored in `src/client/pcf/CommunicationConnections/views/Communications-Awaiting-Association.md` (FetchXML + layoutXML → savedquery on `sprk_communication`).
    4. **Remove the deployed Send web resource + ribbon button** (task 044c retired the source; this removes them from the target env via solution re-import of the emptied CommunicationRibbons OR admin deletion). Keep the Create-To-Do button.
    5. Verify the OOB form still opens normally (reversibility) and both PCFs render.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke deployment + QA engineer. Fluent with `pac` (pcf push / solution import), model-driven form customization, and browser UI testing of PCFs on model-driven forms.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Both PCFs deployed to the dev environment and placed on the OOB `sprk_communication` form (Connections in the accessories column, Actions in the command area); the "Communications Awaiting Association" view exists and is matter-level auth-scoped; the deployed Send web resource + ribbon button are removed (Create-To-Do retained); the OOB form opens correctly. UI verification confirms: Connections renders the review slots + confirm/primary/create-from-email; Actions renders Reply/Forward/Send/Save/Save-to-SharePoint and the composer opens; dark + light mode (ADR-021). Failures fixed or filed as deferrals.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      W4 pivot: enhance the OOB form with PCFs rather than replace it with a Code Page. 042 built CommunicationConnections (+ the view); 044 built CommunicationActions (+ the /{id}/archive endpoint) and retired the ribbon Send source. This task deploys both PCFs, wires the form, packs the view, and removes the deployed Send button — closing Wave 4. Higher-risk because it changes a live form + removes a deployed button; a confirmed OOB-form-still-opens fallback is the acceptance bar.
    </background>
